# Marker & skeleton/rig placement checks

Never bind, retune wear, or mark `skeleton_seen` from numbers alone. Critical landmarks must be **zoomed on the mesh** in both Markers and Skeleton/Rig views.

## Order (hard)

1. **Markers** — zoom each critical 8-dot → confirm on anatomy
2. **Skeleton / Rig** — zoom each critical joint/bone end on the mesh → confirm inside/on the body
3. **Bind** — only after both pass
4. **Wear / paint** — only after markers + skeleton are trusted
5. Do not change wear to “fix” a bad chin/crown/shoulder/knee joint

## Zoom Markers (eight dots)

- **Chin** — jaw tip / under lip, **not** mid-face (mouth/nose). Prefer the user’s hand-placed chin over auto when they disagree; defaults were fixed to target the jaw, but always zoom-check.
- **Neck base** — sternum pit under the collarbones, not up under the chin.
- **Clavicles** — from neck pit out toward the shoulders; **upperarm** in the deltoid socket on the body.
- **Head region via chin** — drives neck/head; wrong chin height misplaces the whole head chain.
- **Groin** — crotch height, not mid-belly or mid-thigh.
- **Elbows / wrists / knees** — true joint crease, not mid-limb.

## Zoom Skeleton / Rig (joints on mesh)

Open Skeleton (or Rig with bones visible) and **orbit/zoom onto each joint** so the bone end is large in frame. On the Rig screen, turn on **Blender bones** so you see the real Blender bone positions on the mesh — not only the colored joint dots. Confirm each sits **on/inside the mesh**, not floating in hair, floating off skin, or buried in the wrong limb:

| Joint | Must sit |
|-------|----------|
| neck / neck_base | In the neck column, above shoulders |
| head / head_top | Skull center and crown — crown near mesh top, not mid-face or in ponytail only |
| clavicle_l/r | Collarbone / shoulder root on the torso |
| upperarm / lowerarm / hand | Inside the arm volume; hand not past mitt tip oddly |
| spine_01..03 / pelvis | Torso core depth (not breast tip, not back hair) |
| thigh / calf / foot | Inside the leg; knee at crease |

Also check left/right symmetry in close-up when both sides are editable.

## How to zoom

- Studio window open: Markers first, then Skeleton/Rig — zoom each listed joint, screenshot the close-up, **read the image**.
- Prefer joint close-ups over full-body frames — full-body hides mid-face chin and floating clavicles.
- Headless/API: run `off_body` / `z/H` checks, then still get zoomed Markers **and** Skeleton/Rig shots of head, shoulders, hips, knees before `see_skeleton` or `rig`.

## After a marker or joint move

- Recompute joints from the eight dots when markers change (no stale `head_top`).
- Keep mittens when the mesh has no T-pose finger splay.
- Re-zoom the **same** marker and the **driven skeleton joints** after the write.
- Only then `see_skeleton` / bind.
